{
  "title": "34: Sabaa سبإ",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nاَلْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ الَّذِىْ لَهٗ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِ وَلَهُ الْحَمْدُ فِى الْاٰخِرَةِ ؕ وَهُوَ الْحَكِيْمُ الْخَبِيْرُ‏(1)\nAALHAMDU LILLAAHE LAZEE LAHU MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZE LAHUL HAMDO FIL AAKHERATE WA HOWA HAKEEM KHABEER.\nPraise be to Allah, to Whom belong all things in the heavens and on earth: to Him be Praise in the Hereafter: and He is Full of Wisdom, acquainted with all things. \nيَعْلَمُ مَا يَلِجُ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَمَا يَخْرُجُ مِنْهَا وَمَا يَنْزِلُ مِنَ السَّمَآءِ وَمَا يَعْرُجُ فِيْهَا ؕ وَهُوَ الرَّحِيْمُ الْغَفُوْرُ‏(2)\nYA’LAMO MAA YALEJU FIL ARZE WA MAA YAKHROJO MINHAA WA MAA YANZELU MENAL SAMAAA-E WA MAA YAA’RUJU FEEHAA WA HOWA RAHEEM GHAFOORUL.\nHe knows all that goes into the earth, and all that comes out thereof; all that comes down from the sky and all that ascends thereto and He is the Most Merciful, the Oft-Forgiving. \nوَقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا لَا تَاْتِيْنَا السَّاعَةُ ؕ قُلْ بَلٰى وَرَبِّىْ لَتَاْتِيَنَّكُمْۙ عٰلِمِ الْغَيْبِ ۚ لَا يَعْزُبُ عَنْهُ مِثْقَالُ ذَرَّةٍ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَلَا فِى الْاَرْضِ وَلَاۤ اَصْغَرُ مِنْ ذٰ لِكَ وَلَاۤ اَكْبَرُ اِلَّا فِىْ كِتٰبٍ مُّبِيْنٍۙ‏(3)\nWA QAALA LAZEENA KAFAROO LAA TAATEENAA SAA-A’TO QUL BALAA WA RABBEE LATAATEENNAKUM A’ALEMIL GHAYBE LAA YAA’ZUBU A’NHO MESQAALU ZARRATIN FIL SAMAAWAATE WA LAA FIL ARZE WA LAA AASGHARU MIN ZAA LEKA WA LAA AKBARO ILLAA FEE KETAABIM MOBEEN.\nThe Unbelievers say, “Never to us will come the Hour”: Say, “Nay! but most surely, by my Lord, it will come upon you;- by Him Who knows the unseen, from Whom is not hidden the least little atom in the heavens or on earth: Nor is there anything less than that, or greater, but is in the Record Perspicuous: \nلِّيَجْزِىَ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوا وَعَمِلُوْا الصّٰلِحٰتِؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ لَهُمْ مَّغْفِرَةٌ وَّرِزْقٌ كَرِيْمٌ‏(4)\nLE-YAJZEYAL LAZEENA AAMANUT AAMANOO AS-SAALEHAATE OOLAAA-EKA LAHUM MAGHFERATUNW WWAREZQUN KAREEM.\nThat He may reward those who believe and work deeds of righteousness: for such is Forgiveness and a Sustenance Most Generous.” \nوَالَّذِيْنَ سَعَوْ فِىْۤ اٰيٰتِنَا مُعٰجِزِيْنَ اُولٰٓئِكَ لَهُمْ عَذَابٌ مِّنْ رِّجْزٍ اَلِيْمٌ‏(5)\nWAL LAZEENA SAA’AW FEE AAYAATENAA MUA’AAJEZEENA OOLAAA-EKA LAHUM A’ZAABUN MIN RREJZIN ALEEM.\nBut those who strive against Our Signs, to frustrate them, for such will be a Penalty, a Punishment most humiliating. \nوَيَرَى الَّذِيْنَ اُوْتُوا الْعِلْمَ الَّذِىْۤ اُنْزِلَ اِلَيْكَ مِنْ رَّبِّكَ هُوَ الْحَقَّ ۙ وَيَهْدِىْۤ اِلٰى صِرَاطِ الْعَزِيْزِ الْحَمِيْدِ‏(6)\nWA YARAL LAZEENA OOTUL OOTUL I’LMA LAZEE UNZELA ELAYKA MIN RABBEKA HOWA HAQQA WA YAHDEE ELAA SERAATE A’ZEEZIL HAMEEDIL.\nAnd those to whom knowledge has come see that the (Revelation) sent down to thee from thy Lord - that is the Truth, and that it guides to the Path of the Exalted (in might), Worthy of all praise. \nوَقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا هَلْ نَدُلُّكُمْ عَلٰى رَجُلٍ يُّنَبِّئُكُمْ اِذَا مُزِّقْتُمْ كُلَّ مُمَزَّقٍۙ اِنَّكُمْ لَفِىْ خَلْقٍ جَدِيْدٍۚ‏(7)\nWA QAALA LAZEENA KAFAROO HAL NADULLUKUM A’LAA RAJULIN YYUNABBEUKUM EZAA MUZZEQTUM KULLA MUMAZZAQIN INNAKUM LAFEE KHALQIN JADEEDIN.\nThe Unbelievers say (in ridicule): “Shall we point out to you a man that will tell you, when ye are all scattered to pieces in disintegration, that ye shall (then be raised) in a New Creation? \nاَ فْتَرٰى عَلَى اللّٰهِ كَذِبًا اَمْ بِهٖ جِنَّةٌ  ؕ بَلِ الَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِالْاٰخِرَةِ فِى الْعَذَابِ وَالضَّلٰلِ الْبَعِيْدِ‏(8)\nA’ZAABAN FTARAA A’LAL LAAHE KAZEBAN AM BEHI JENNATUN BALIL LAZEENA LAA YOAMENOONA BIL AAKHERATE FIL A’ZAABE WAALZZALAALE AL-BAE’EEDE.\n“Has he invented a falsehood against Allah, or has a spirit (seized) him?”- Nay, it is those who believe not in the Hereafter, that are in (real) Penalty, and in farthest error. \nاَفَلَمْ يَرَوْا اِلٰى مَا بَيْنَ اَيْدِيْهِمْ وَمَا خَلْفَهُمْ مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ وَالْاَرْضِ ؕ اِنْ نَّشَاْ نَخْسِفْ بِهِمُ الْاَرْضَ اَوْ نُسْقِطْ عَلَيْهِمْ كِسَفًا مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيَةً لِّكُلِّ عَبْدٍ مُّنِيْبٍ‏(9)\nA-FALAM YARAW ELAA MAA BAYNA AYDEEHIM WA MAA KHALFAHUM MENAL SAMAAA-E WAL ARZE IN NASHAA NAKHSEF BEHEMUL ARZA AW NUSQET A’LAYHIM KESAFAN MENAL SAMAAA-E INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYATAL LEKULLE A’ABDIN MMUNEEBIN.\nSee they not what is before them and behind them, of the sky and the earth? If We wished, We could cause the earth to swallow them up, or cause a piece of the sky to fall upon them. Verily in this is a Sign for every devotee that turns to Allah (in repentance). \nوَلَقَدْ اٰتَيْنَا دَاوٗدَ مِنَّا فَضْلًا ؕ يٰجِبَالُ اَوِّبِىْ مَعَهٗ وَالطَّيْرَ ۚ وَاَلَنَّا لَهُ الْحَدِيْدَ ۙ‏(10)\nWA LAQAD AATAYNAA DAAWOODA MINNAA FAZLAM YAAJEBAALU AAWBEAA MA-A’HU WA TAYRA WAALANNAA LAHUL AL-HADEEDA.\nWe bestowed Grace aforetime on David from ourselves: “O ye Mountains! Sing ye back the Praises of Allah with him! and ye birds (also)! And We made the iron soft for him;- \nاَنِ اعْمَلْ سٰبِغٰتٍ وَّقَدِّرْ فِى السَّرْدِ وَاعْمَلُوْا صَالِحًا ؕ اِنِّىْ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ بَصِيْرٌ‏(11)\nSAALEHAN AA’MAL SAABEGHAATIN WWAQADDER FIL AS-SARDE WAAA’MALOOA SAALEHAN INNEE BEMAA TA’MALOON BASEER.\n(Commanding), “Make thou coast of mail, balancing well the rings of chain armour, and work ye righteousness; for be sure I see (clearly) all that ye do.” \nوَلِسُلَيْمٰنَ الرِّيْحَ غُدُوُّهَا شَهْرٌ وَّرَوَاحُهَا شَهْرٌۚ وَ اَسَلْنَا لَهٗ عَيْنَ الْقِطْرِؕ وَمِنَ الْجِنِّ مَنْ يَّعْمَلُ بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ بِاِذْنِ رَبِّهِؕ وَمَنْ يَّزِغْ مِنْهُمْ عَنْ اَمْرِنَا نُذِقْهُ مِنْ عَذَابِ السَّعِيْرِ‏(12)\nWA LESOLAYMAANA AR-REEHA GHUDOOHAA SHAHRUN WWARAWAAHUHAA SHAHRUN WA AASALNAA LAHU A’YNAL AL-QETRE WA MENAN JINNE MAN YYAA’MALU BAYNA YADAYHE BE-IZNIL RABBEHE WA MAN YYAZEGH MINHUM A’N AAMRENAA NUZEQHU MIN A’ZAABIN SA-E’ER.\nAnd to Solomon (We made) the Wind (obedient): Its early morning (stride) was a month's (journey), and its evening (stride) was a month's (journey); and We made a Font of molten brass to flow for him; and there were Jinns that worked in front of him, by the leave of his Lord, and if any of them turned aside from our command, We made him taste of the Penalty of the Blazing Fire. \nيَعْمَلُوْنَ لَهٗ مَا يَشَآءُ مِنْ مَّحَارِيْبَ وَتَمَاثِيْلَ وَجِفَانٍ كَالْجَوَابِ وَقُدُوْرٍ رّٰسِيٰتٍ ؕ اِعْمَلُوْۤا اٰلَ دَاوٗدَ شُكْرًا ؕ وَقَلِيْلٌ مِّنْ عِبَادِىَ الشَّكُوْرُ‏(13)\nYA’MALOON LAHU MAA YASHAAA MIN MMAHAAREEBA WATAMAASEELA WAJEFAANIN KAALJAWAABE WAQUDOORIN RRAASEETIN AEA’MALOOA AALA DAAWOODA SHUKRAN WA QALEELUM MIN E’EBAADEAAA ASH-SHAKOORU.\nThey worked for him as he desired, (making) arches, images, basons as large as reservoirs, and (cooking) cauldrons fixed (in their places): “Work ye, sons of David, with thanks! but few of My servants are grateful!” \nفَلَمَّا قَضَيْنَا عَلَيْهِ الْمَوْتَ مَا دَلَّهُمْ عَلٰى مَوْتِهٖۤ اِلَّا دَآ بَّةُ الْاَرْضِ تَاْ كُلُ مِنْسَاَتَهُ ۚ فَلَمَّا خَرَّ تَبَيَّنَتِ الْجِنُّ اَنْ لَّوْ كَانُوْا يَعْلَمُوْنَ الْغَيْبَ مَا لَبِثُوْا فِى الْعَذَابِ الْمُهِيْنِ ؕ‏(14)\nFALAMMAA QAZAYNAA A’LAYHE MAWTA MAA DALLAHUM A’LAA MAWTEH ILLAA DAABBATINW BBATU ARZE TAA KULU MENSAATAHU FALAMMAA KHARRA TABAYNATE AL-JENNU AN LAW KAANOO YA’LAMOON GHAYBA MAA MAA FIL A’ZAABE MOHEENE.\nThen, when We decreed (Solomon's) death, nothing showed them his death except a little worm of the earth, which kept (slowly) gnawing away at his staff: so when he fell down, the Jinns saw plainly that if they had known the unseen, they would not have tarried in the humiliating Penalty (of their Task). \nلَقَدْ كَانَ لِسَبَاٍ فِىْ مَسْكَنِهِمْ اٰيَةٌ  ۚ جَنَّتٰنِ عَنْ يَّمِيْنٍ وَّشِمَالٍ ؕ  کُلُوْا مِنْ رِّزْقِ رَبِّكُمْ وَاشْكُرُوْا لَهٗ ؕ بَلْدَةٌ طَيِّبَةٌ وَّرَبٌّ غَفُوْرٌ‏‏(15)\nLAQAD KAANA LE-SABA-IM FEE MASKANEHEM TAA-TEENAA JANNATAAN A’N YYAMEENIN WWASHEMAALIN LOOA MIN RIZQIL RABBEKUM WASH KOROO LAHU BALDATUN TAYBATUN WWARABBUN GHAFOORUR.\nThere was, for Saba, aforetime, a Sign in their home-land - two Gardens to the right and to the left. “Eat of the Sustenance (provided) by your Lord, and be grateful to Him: a territory fair and happy, and a Lord Oft-Forgiving! \nفَاَعْرَضُوْا فَاَرْسَلْنَا عَلَيْهِمْ سَيْلَ الْعَرِمِ وَبَدَّلْنٰهُمْ بِجَنَّتَيْهِمْ جَنَّتَيْنِ ذَوَاتَىْ اُكُلٍ خَمْطٍ وَّاَثْلٍ وَّشَىْءٍ مِّنْ سِدْرٍ قَلِيْلٍ‏(16)\nFA A-A’RAZOO FA-ARSALNAA A’LAYHIM SAYLA AL-A’AREME WABADDALNAAHUM BEJANNATAYHEM JANNATAYNE ZAWAATAA AUKULIN KHAMTIN WWAASLIN WWASHAAIN MIN SIDRIM QALEELIN.\nBut they turned away (from Allah), and We sent against them the Flood (released) from the dams, and We converted their two garden (rows) into “gardens” producing bitter fruit, and tamarisks, and some few (stunted) Lote-trees. \nذٰ لِكَ جَزَيْنٰهُمْ بِمَا كَفَرُوْا ؕ وَهَلْ نُجٰزِىْۤ اِلَّا الْكَفُوْرَ‏(17)\nZAA LEKA JAZAYNAAHUM BEMAA KAFAROO WA HAL NUJAAZEAA ILLAA AL-KAFOORA.\nThat was the Requital We gave them because they ungratefully rejected Faith: and never do We give (such) requital except to such as are ungrateful rejecters. \nوَجَعَلْنَا بَيْنَهُمْ وَبَيْنَ الْقُرَى الَّتِىْ بٰرَكْنَا فِيْهَا قُرًى ظَاهِرَةً وَّقَدَّرْنَا فِيْهَا السَّيْرَ ؕ سِيْرُوْا فِيْهَا لَيَالِىَ وَاَيَّامًا اٰمِنِيْنَ‏(18)\nWA JA-A’LNAA BAYNAHUM WA BAYNA AL-QURAA LATEE BAARAKNAA FEEHAA QORAM ZAAHERATAN WWAQADDARNAA FEEHAA AS-SAYRA SEEROO FEEHAA LAYAALEAAA WA ILLAA AAMENEENA.\nBetween them and the Cities on which We had poured our blessings, We had placed Cities in prominent positions, and between them We had appointed stages of journey in due proportion: “Travel therein, secure, by night and by day.” \nفَقَالُوْا رَبَّنَا بٰعِدْ بَيْنَ اَسْفَارِنَا وَظَلَمُوْۤا اَنْفُسَهُمْ فَجَعَلْنٰهُمْ اَحَادِيْثَ وَمَزَّقْنٰهُمْ كُلَّ مُمَزَّقٍ ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيٰتٍ لِّكُلِّ صَبَّارٍ شَكُوْرٍ‏(19)\nFA-QAALOO RABBANAA BAAE’ED BAYNA AASFAARENAA WA ZALAMOO ANFOSAHUM FAJAA’ALNAAHUM AAHAADEESA WAMAZZAQNAAHUM KULLA MUMAZZAQIN INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYAATIL LEKULLE SABBAARIN SHAKOORIN.\nBut they said: “Our Lord! Place longer distances between our journey-stages”: but they wronged themselves (therein). At length We made them as a tale (that is told), and We dispersed them all in scattered fragments. Verily in this are Signs for every (soul that is) patiently constant and grateful. \nوَلَقَدْ صَدَّقَ عَلَيْهِمْ اِبْلِيْسُ ظَنَّهٗ فَاتَّبَعُوْهُ اِلَّا فَرِيْقًا مِّنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(20)\nWA LAQAD SADDAQA A’LAYHIM AEBLEESU ZANNAH FAATTABAU’OOHU ILLAA FAREEQAM MENAL MOAMENEEN.\nAnd on them did Satan prove true his idea, and they followed him, all but a party that believed. \nوَمَا كَانَ لَهٗ عَلَيْهِمْ مِّنْ سُلْطٰنٍ اِلَّا لِنَعْلَمَ مَنْ يُّؤْمِنُ بِالْاٰخِرَةِ مِمَّنْ هُوَ مِنْهَا فِىْ شَكٍّ ؕ وَ رَبُّكَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ حَفِيْظٌ‏(21)\nWA MAA KAANA LAHU A’LAYHIM MIN SULTAANIN ILLAA ILLAA MAN YOAMENO BIL AAKHERATE MIMMAN HOWA MINHAA FEE SHAKKIM WA RABBOKA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN HAFEEZUN.\nBut he had no authority over them, except that We might test the man who believes in the Hereafter from him who is in doubt concerning it: and thy Lord doth watch over all things. \nقُلِ ادْعُوا الَّذِيْنَ زَعَمْتُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِۚ لَا يَمْلِكُوْنَ مِثْقَالَ ذَرَّةٍ فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَلَا فِى الْاَرْضِ وَمَا لَهُمْ فِيْهِمَا مِنْ شِرْكٍ وَّمَا لَهٗ مِنْهُمْ مِّنْ ظَهِيْرٍ‏(22)\nQOLIL ADU’OOA LAZEENA ZA-A’MTUM MIN DOONIL LAAHE LAA YAMLEKOONA MISQAALA ZARRATIN FIL SAMAAWAATE WA LAA FIL ARZE WA MAA LAHUM FEEHEMAA MIN SHERKIN WA MAA LAHU MINHUM MIN ZAHEERIN.\nSay: “Call upon other (gods) whom ye fancy, besides Allah: They have no power, not the weight of an atom, in the heavens or on earth: No (sort of) share have they therein, nor is any of them a helper to Allah. \nوَلَا تَنْفَعُ الشَّفَاعَةُ عِنْدَهٗۤ اِلَّا لِمَنْ اَذِنَ لَهٗ ؕ حَتّٰٓى اِذَا فُزِّعَ عَنْ قُلُوْبِهِمْ قَالُوْا مَاذَا ۙ قَالَ رَبُّكُمْ ؕ قَالُوا الْحَقَّ ۚ وَهُوَ الْعَلِىُّ الْكَبِيْرُ‏(23)\nWA LAA TANFAU’U ASH-SHAFAAA’ATU I’NDAHU ILLAA LEMAN-Y AZENA LAHU HATTAA EZAA FUZZEA’A A’N QOLOOBEHIM QAALOO MAA QAALA RABBOKUM QAALUD HAQQA WA HOWA A’LIYYUL AL-KABEERU.\n“No intercession can avail in His Presence, except for those for whom He has granted permission. So far (is this the case) that, when terror is removed from their hearts (at the Day of Judgment, then) will they say, 'what is it that your Lord commanded?' they will say, 'That which is true and just; and He is the Most High Most Great'.” \nقُلْ مَنْ يَّرْزُقُكُمْ مِّنَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِؕ قُلِ اللّٰهُ ۙ وَ اِنَّاۤ اَوْ اِيَّاكُمْ لَعَلٰى هُدًى اَوْ فِىْ ضَلٰلٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(24)\nQUL MAN YARZOQOKUM MENAL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZ QOLIL LAAHO WA INNAA AW AEEAKUM LAA’ALAA HODAM AW FEE ZALAALIM MOBEEN.\nSay: “Who gives you sustenance, from the heavens and the earth?” Say: “It is Allah; and certain it is that either we or ye are on right guidance or in manifest error!” \nقُلْ لَّا تُسْئَلُوْنَ عَمَّاۤ اَجْرَمْنَا وَلَا نُسْئَلُ عَمَّا تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(25)\nQUL LAA TUS-ALOONA A’MMAA AAJRAMNAA WA LAA NUSALU A’MMAA TA’MALOON.\nSay: “Ye shall not be questioned as to our sins, nor shall we be questioned as to what ye do.” \nقُلْ يَجْمَعُ بَيْنَنَا رَبُّنَا ثُمَّ يَفْتَحُ بَيْنَنَا بِالْحَقِّ ؕ وَهُوَ الْفَتَّاحُ الْعَلِيْمُ‏(26)\nQUL YAJMAU’U BAYNANAA RABBONAA SUMMA YAFTAHU BAYNANAA BIL-HAQQE WA HOWA AL-FATTAAHU A’LEEM.\nSay: “Our Lord will gather us together and will in the end decide the matter between us (and you) in truth and justice: and He is the one to decide, the One Who knows all.” \nقُلْ اَرُوْنِىَ الَّذِيْنَ اَ لْحَقْتُمْ بِهٖ شُرَكَآءَ كَلَّا ؕ بَلْ هُوَ اللّٰهُ الْعَزِيْزُ الْحَكِيْمُ‏(27)\nQUL AAROONEAAA LAZEENA A’ZAABAN LHAQTUM BEHI SHORA-KAAA-A KALLAA BAL HOWA LAAHO A’ZEEZUL HAKEEM.\nSay: “Show me those whom ye have joined with Him as partners: by no means (can ye). Nay, He is Allah, the Exalted in Power, the Wise.” \nوَمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنٰكَ اِلَّا كَآفَّةً لِّلنَّاسِ بَشِيْرًا وَّنَذِيْرًا وَّلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَ النَّاسِ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(28)\nWA MAA ARSALNAAKA ILLAA KAAAF-FATANW LIN-NAASE BASHEERANW WA NAZEERANW WA LAAKINNA AKSARAN NAASE LAA YA’LAMOON.\nWe have not sent thee but as a universal (Messenger) to men, giving them glad tidings, and warning them (against sin), but most men understand not. \nوَيَقُوْلُوْنَ مَتٰى هٰذَا الْوَعْدُ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(29)\nWA YAQOOLOONA MATAA HAAZAA WA’DO IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\nThey say: “When will this promise (come to pass) if ye are telling the truth?” \nقُلْ لَّكُمْ مِّيْعَادُ يَوْمٍ لَّا تَسْتَاْخِرُوْنَ عَنْهُ سَاعَةً وَّلَا تَسْتَقْدِمُوْنَ‏(30)\nQUL LAKUM MMEEA’AADU YAWMIN LAA TASTAAKHEROONA A’NHO SAAA’ATAN WA LAA TASTAQDEMOONA.\nSay: “The appointment to you is for a Day, which ye cannot put back for an hour nor put forward.” \nوَقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا لَنْ نُّؤْمِنَ بِهٰذَا الْقُرْاٰنِ وَلَا بِالَّذِىْ بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِؕ وَلَوْ تَرٰٓى اِذِ الظّٰلِمُوْنَ مَوْقُوْفُوْنَ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْۖۚ يَرْجِعُ بَعْضُهُمْ اِلٰى بَعْضِ اۨلْقَوْلَ‌ۚ يَقُوْلُ الَّذِيْنَ اسْتُضْعِفُوْا لِلَّذِيْنَ اسْتَكْبَرُوْا لَوْلَاۤ اَنْتُمْ لَكُنَّا مُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(31)\nWA QAALA LAZEENA KAFAROO LAN NOAMENA BEHAAZAA QUR-AANE WA LAA BIL-LAZEE BAYNA YADAYHE WA LAW TARAAA EZIM ZAALEMOON MAWQOOFOONA I’NDAL RABBEHIM YARJE-O’L KHALAA ELAA BAA’ZE QAWLA YAQOOLO LAZEENA TUZ-E’FOO LILLAZEENA ASTAKBAROOA LAWLAA ANTUM LAKUNNAA MUMENEENA.\nThe Unbelievers say: “We shall neither believe in this scripture nor in (any) that (came) before it.” Couldst thou but see when the wrong-doers will be made to stand before their Lord, throwing back the word (of blame) on one another! Those who had been despised will say to the arrogant ones: “Had it not been for you, we should certainly have been believers!” \nقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ اسْتَكْبَرُوْا لِلَّذِيْنَ اسْتُضْعِفُوْۤا اَنَحْنُ صَدَدْنٰكُمْ عَنِ الْهُدٰى بَعْدَ اِذْ جَآءَكُمْ بَلْ كُنْتُمْ مُّجْرِمِيْنَ‏(32)\nQAALA LAZEENA ASTAKBAROOA LILLAZEENA TUZ-E’FOO AANAHNU SADADNAAKUM A’NIL HODAA BA’DA IZ JAAA-AKUM BAL KUNTUM MMUJREMEENA.\nThe arrogant ones will say to those who had been despised: “Was it we who kept you back from Guidance after it reached you? Nay, rather, it was ye who transgressed. \nوَقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ اسْتُضْعِفُوْا لِلَّذِيْنَ اسْتَكْبَرُوْا بَلْ مَكْرُ الَّيْلِ وَ النَّهَارِ اِذْ تَاْمُرُوْنَنَاۤ اَنْ نَّكْفُرَ بِاللّٰهِ وَنَجْعَلَ لَهٗۤ اَنْدَادًا ؕ وَاَسَرُّوا النَّدَامَةَ لَمَّا رَاَوُا الْعَذَابَ ؕ وَجَعَلْنَا الْاَغْلٰلَ فِىْۤ اَعْنَاقِ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا ؕ هَلْ يُجْزَوْنَ اِلَّا مَا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(33)\nWA QAALA LAZEENA TUZ-E’FOO LILLAZEENA ASTAKBAROOA BAL MAKRU LAYLE WA AN-NAHAARE IZ TAAMUROONANAA AN NNAKFURA BIL-LAAHE WANAJA’ALA LAHU ANDAADANW WAASARROOA AN-NADAAMATA LAMMAA RAAWUA A’ZAABA WA JA-A’LNAA AL-AAGHLAALA FEE AAA’NAAQE LAZEENA KAFAROO HAL YUJZAWNA ILLAA MAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nThose who had been despised will say to the arrogant ones: “Nay! it was a plot (of yours) by day and by night: Behold! Ye (constantly) ordered us to be ungrateful to Allah and to attribute equals to Him!” They will declare (their) repentance when they see the Penalty: We shall put yokes on the necks of the Unbelievers: It would only be a requital for their (ill) Deeds. \nوَمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنَا فِىْ قَرْيَةٍ مِّنْ نَّذِيْرٍ اِلَّا قَالَ مُتْرَفُوْهَاۤ ۙاِنَّا بِمَاۤ اُرْسِلْتُمْ بِهٖ كٰفِرُوْنَ‏(34)\nWA MAA ARSALNAA FEE QARYATINW MIN NAZEERIM ILLAA QAALA MUTRAFOOHAA INNAA BEMAA URSILTUM BEHI KAAFEROON.\nNever did We send a warner to a population, but the wealthy ones among them said: “We believe not in the (Message) with which ye have been sent.” \nوَ قَالُوْا نَحْنُ اَكْثَرُ اَمْوَالًا وَّاَوْلَادًا ۙ وَّمَا نَحْنُ بِمُعَذَّبِيْنَ‏(35)\nWA QAALOO NAHNO AAKSARU AAMWAALAN WWAAWLAADAN WA MAA NAHNO BEMUA’AZZABEENA.\nThey said: “We have more in wealth and in sons, and we cannot be punished.” \nقُلْ اِنَّ رَبِّىْ يَبْسُطُ الرِّزْقَ لِمَنْ يَّشَآءُ وَيَقْدِرُ وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَ النَّاسِ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(36)\nQUL INNAL RABBEE YABSOTUR RIZQA LEMAN-Y YASHAAA-O WA LAAKINNAL AKSARAN NAASE LAA YA’LAMOON.\nSay: “Verily my Lord enlarges and restricts the Provision to whom He pleases, but most men understand not.” \nوَمَاۤ اَمْوَالُكُمْ وَلَاۤ اَوْلَادُكُمْ بِالَّتِىْ تُقَرِّبُكُمْ عِنْدَنَا زُلْفٰٓى اِلَّا مَنْ اٰمَنَ وَعَمِلَ صَالِحًا فَاُولٰٓئِكَ لَهُمْ جَزَآءُ الضِّعْفِ بِمَا عَمِلُوْا وَهُمْ فِى الْغُرُفٰتِ اٰمِنُوْنَ‏(37)\nWA MAA AMWAALOKUM WA LAA LAA AWLAADOKUM BIL-LATEE TUQARREBUKUM E’ENDANAA ZULFAAA ILLAA MAN AAMANA WA A’MELA SAALEHAN FA-OOLAAA-EKA LAHUM JAZAAA-O AZ-ZEA’FE BEMAA A’MELOO WA HUM FIL AL-GHURUFAATE AAMENOON.\nIt is not your wealth nor your sons, that will bring you nearer to Us in degree: but only those who believe and work righteousness - these are the ones for whom there is a multiplied Reward for their deeds, while secure they (reside) in the dwellings on high! \nوَ الَّذِيْنَ يَسْعَوْنَ فِىْۤ اٰيٰتِنَا مُعٰجِزِيْنَ اُولٰٓئِكَ فِى الْعَذَابِ مُحْضَرُوْنَ‏(38)\nWA LAZEENA YASA’AWNA FEE AAYAATENAA MUA’AAJEZEENA OOLAAA-EKA FIL A’ZAABE MOHZAROON.\nThose who strive against Our Signs, to frustrate them, will be given over into Punishment. \nقُلْ اِنَّ رَبِّىْ يَبْسُطُ الرِّزْقَ لِمَنْ يَّشَآءُ مِنْ عِبَادِهٖ وَيَقْدِرُ لَهٗ ؕ وَمَاۤ اَنْفَقْتُمْ مِّنْ شَىْءٍ فَهُوَ يُخْلِفُهٗ ۚ وَهُوَ خَيْرُ الرّٰزِقِيْنَ‏(39)\nQUL INNAL RABBEE YABSOTUR RIZQA LEMAN-Y YASHAAA-O MIN E’BAADEHI WA LAHU WA MAA ANFAQTUM MIN SHAY-IN FAHOWA YUKHLEFUH WA HOWA KHAYRUR RAAZEQEEN.\nSay: “Verily my Lord enlarges and restricts the Sustenance to such of his servants as He pleases: and nothing do ye spend in the least (in His cause) but He replaces it: for He is the Best of those who grant Sustenance. \nوَيَوْمَ يَحْشُرُهُمْ جَمِيْعًا ثُمَّ يَقُوْلُ لِلْمَلٰٓئِكَةِ اَهٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ اِيَّاكُمْ كَانُوْا يَعْبُدُوْنَ‏(40)\nWA YAWMA YAHSHURUHUM JAMEE-A’A SUMMA YAQOOLO LIL-MALAAA-EKATE AAHAAAULAAE AEEAKUM KAANOO YA’BODOON.\nOne Day He will gather them all together, and say to the angels, “Was it you that these men used to worship?” \nقَالُوْا سُبْحٰنَكَ اَنْتَ وَلِيُّنَا مِنْ دُوْنِهِمْۚ بَلْ كَانُوْا يَعْبُدُوْنَ الْجِنَّ ۚ اَكْثَرُهُمْ بِهِمْ مُّؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(41)\nQAALOO SUBHAANAKA ANTA WALEENAA MIN DOONEHEM BAL KAANOO YA’BODOON AL-JENNA AKSAROHUM BEHIM REJAALUM.\nThey will say, “Glory to Thee! our (tie) is with Thee - as Protector - not with them. Nay, but they worshipped the Jinns: most of them believed in them.” \nفَالْيَوْمَ لَا يَمْلِكُ بَعْضُكُمْ لِبَعْضٍ نَّفْعًا وَّلَا ضَرًّا ؕ وَنَقُوْلُ لِلَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا ذُوْقُوْا عَذَابَ النَّارِ الَّتِىْ كُنْتُمْ بِهَا تُكَذِّبُوْنَ‏(42)\nFALYAWMA LAA YAMLEKU BA’ZOKUM LE-BA’ZIN NNAFA’AN WA LAA BEKUM WANAQOOLU LILLAZEENA ZALAMOO ZOOQOO A’ZAABAL NAAR LATEE KUNTUM BEHAA TOKAZZEBOON.\nSo on that Day no power shall they have over each other, for profit or harm: and We shall say to the wrong-doers, “Taste ye the Penalty of the Fire, the which ye were wont to deny!” \nوَاِذَا تُتْلٰى عَلَيْهِمْ اٰيٰتُنَا بَيِّنٰتٍ قَالُوْا مَا هٰذَاۤ اِلَّا رَجُلٌ يُّرِيْدُ اَنْ يَّصُدَّكُمْ عَمَّا كَانَ يَعْبُدُ اٰبَآؤُكُمْ‌ ۚ وَقَالُوْا مَا هٰذَاۤ اِلَّاۤ اِفْكٌ مُّفْتَرً ىؕ وَقَالَ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا لِلْحَقِّ لَمَّا جَآءَهُمْ ۙ اِنْ هٰذَاۤ اِلَّا سِحْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‏(43)\nWA EZAA TUTLAA A’LAYHIM AAYAATONAA BAYYENAAT QAALOO MAA HAAZAA ILLAA RAJOLUM YYUREEDU AN YYASUDDAKUM A’MMAA KAANA YAA’BUDU AAABAAUKUM WA QAALOO MAA HAAZAA ILLAA AEFKUN MMUFTARAN AA WA QAALA LAZEENA KAFAROO LIL-HAQQE LAMMAA JAAA-AHUM IN HAAZAA ILLAA SEHRUM MOBEEN.\nWhen Our Clear Signs are rehearsed to them, they say, “This is only a man who wishes to hinder you from the (worship) which your fathers practised.” And they say, “This is only a falsehood invented!” and the Unbelievers say of the Truth when it comes to them, “This is nothing but evident magic!” \nوَمَاۤ اٰتَيْنٰهُمْ مِّنْ كُتُبٍ يَّدْرُسُوْنَهَا وَمَاۤ اَرْسَلْنَاۤ اِلَيْهِمْ قَبْلَكَ مِنْ نَّذِيْرٍؕ‏(44)\nWA MAA AATAYNAAHUM MIN KUTUBIN YYADRUSOONAHAA WA MAA ARSALNAA ELAYHIM QABLAKA MIN NNAZEERIN.\nBut We had not given them Books which they could study, nor sent messengers to them before thee as Warners. \nوَكَذَّبَ الَّذِيْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْۙ وَمَا بَلَغُوْا مِعْشَارَ مَاۤ اٰتَيْنٰهُمْ فَكَذَّبُوْا رُسُلِىْ فَكَيْفَ كَانَ نَكِيْرِ‏(45)\nWA KAZZABA LAZEENA MIN QABLEHIM WA MAA BALAGHOOA MEA’SHAARA MAA AATAYNAAHUM FA KAZZABOO RUSULEAA FA-KAYFA KAANA NAKEER.\nAnd their predecessors rejected (the Truth); these have not received a tenth of what We had granted to those: yet when they rejected My messengers, how (terrible) was My rejection (of them)! \nقُلْ اِنَّمَاۤ اَعِظُكُمْ بِوَاحِدَةٍ ۚ اَنْ تَقُوْمُوْا لِلّٰهِ مَثْنٰى وَفُرَادٰى ثُمَّ تَتَفَكَّرُوْا مَا بِصَاحِبِكُمْ مِّنْ جِنَّةٍ ؕ اِنْ هُوَ اِلَّا نَذِيْرٌ لَّكُمْ بَيْنَ يَدَىْ عَذَابٍ شَدِيْدٍ‏(46)\nQUL INNAMAA AAE’EZUKUM BEWAAHEDATIN AN TAQOOMOOA LILLAAHE MASNAA WAFURAADAA SUMMA TATAFAKKAROOA MAA BESAAHEBEKUM MIN JENNATIN IN HOWA ILLAA NAZEERUM LAKUM BAYNA YADAY A’ZAABIN BAA-SIN.\nSay: “I do admonish you on one point: that ye do stand up before Allah, (It may be) in pairs, or (it may be) singly, and reflect (within yourselves): your Companion is not possessed: he is no less than a warner to you, in face of a terrible Penalty.” \nقُلْ مَا سَاَ لْتُكُمْ مِّنْ اَجْرٍ فَهُوَ لَكُمْ ؕ اِنْ اَجْرِىَ اِلَّا عَلَى اللّٰهِ ۚ وَهُوَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ شَهِيْدٌ‏(47)\nQUL MAA HAQ LTUKUM MIN AAJRIN FAHOWA LAKUM IN AAJREAAA ILLAA A’LAL LAAHE WA HOWA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN WA.\nSay: “No reward do I ask of you: it is (all) in your interest: my reward is only due from Allah: And He is witness to all things.” \nقُلْ اِنَّ رَبِّىْ يَقْذِفُ بِالْحَقِّ‌ۚ عَلَّامُ الْغُيُوْبِ‏(48)\nQUL INNAL RABBEE YAQZEFU BIL-HAQQE A’ALLAAMU AL-GHUYOOBE.\nSay: “Verily my Lord doth cast the (mantle of) Truth (over His servants), He that has full knowledge of (all) that is hidden.” \nقُلْ جَآءَ الْحَقُّ وَمَا يُبْدِئُ الْبَاطِلُ وَمَا يُعِيْدُ‏(49)\nQUL JAAA-A HAQQO WA MAA YUBDEO BAATELO WA MAA YUE’EEDU.\nSay: “The Truth has arrived, and Falsehood neither creates anything new, nor restores anything.” \nقُلْ اِنْ ضَلَلْتُ فَاِنَّمَاۤ اَضِلُّ عَلٰى نَفْسِىْ ۚ وَاِنِ اهْتَدَيْتُ فَبِمَا يُوْحِىْۤ اِلَىَّ رَبِّىْ ؕ اِنَّهٗ سَمِيْعٌ قَرِيْبٌ‏(50)\nQUL IN ZALALTU FA-INNAMAA AAZELLU A’LAA NAFSEE WA ENIS AHTADAYTU FA BEMAA YOOHEAA ELAYYA RABBEE INNAHU SAMEE-U’N QAREEB.\nSay: “If I am astray, I only stray to the loss of my own soul: but if I receive guidance, it is because of the inspiration of my Lord to me: it is He Who hears all things, and is (ever) near.” \nوَلَوْ تَرٰٓى اِذْ فَزِعُوْا فَلَا فَوْتَ وَاُخِذُوْا مِنْ مَّكَانٍ قَرِيْبٍۙ‏(51)\nWA LAW TARAAA IZ FAZEU’OOA FALAA FAWTA WA OKHEZOO MIN MAKAANIM QAREEBIN.\nIf thou couldst but see when they will quake with terror; but then there will be no escape (for them), and they will be seized from a position (quite) near. \nوَّقَالُوْۤا اٰمَنَّا بِهٖ‌ ۚ وَاَنّٰى لَهُمُ التَّنَاوُشُ مِنْ مَّكَانٍۢ بَعِيْدٍ ۖۚ‏(52)\nWA QAALOO AAMANNAA BEHI INSAANO WA LAHOMUL AT-TANAAWUSHU MIN MAKAANIM BA-E’ED.\nAnd they will say, “We do believe (now) in the (Truth)”; but how could they receive (Faith) from a position (so far off, \nوَّقَدْ كَفَرُوْا بِهٖ مِنْ قَبْلُۚ وَيَقْذِفُوْنَ بِالْغَيْبِ مِنْ مَّكَانٍۢ بَعِيْدٍ‌‏(53)\nWWAQAD KAFAROO BEHI MIN QABLO WAYAQZEFOONA BIL-GHAYBE MIN MAKAANIM BA-E’ED.\nSeeing that they did reject Faith (entirely) before, and that they (continually) cast (slanders) on the unseen from a position far off? \nوَحِيْلَ بَيْنَهُمْ وَبَيْنَ مَا يَشْتَهُوْنَ كَمَا فُعِلَ بِاَشْيَاعِهِمْ مِّنْ قَبْلُؕ اِنَّهُمْ كَانُوْا فِىْ شَكٍّ مُّرِيْبٍ‏(54)\nWAHEELA BAYNAHUM WA BAYNA MAA YASHTAHOONA KAMAA FUE’ELA BEAASHYAAE’EHEM MIN QABL WA INNAHUM KAANOO FEE SHAKKIM MMUREEBIN.\nAnd between them and their desires, is placed a barrier, as was done in the past with their partisans: for they were indeed in suspicious (disquieting) doubt. ",
  "merits": "Surah al-Sabaa\nThis is a ‘Makki’ Surah and it has 54 verses. It is narrated that the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) said that whoever recites this Surah, on the Day of Judgement, all the Prophets and Messengers will come to meet him.\nIn a saying from Imam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) it is mentioned that whoever recites Surah Sabaa and [Surah Faatir](A39) at night, he will remain under the protection of Allah (s.w.t.) for the whole night. The reward for reciting this Surah is so great that when it is seen in the book of deeds, the reciter’s heart will be filled with joy.\nWearing this Surah as a talisman or drinking its water removes fear from one’s heart and keeps one safe from enemies and wild animals."
